{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Game Documentation
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
	<h1>Game Documentation</h1>
	<p>Here is the documentation for how to play the game and how the game logic is structured.</p>


	<h2>Flowchart</h2>
	<p>Below is the flowchart that represents the basic flow of the game, from dealing the cards to determining the winner:</p>
	<img src="{{ asset('images/flowchart.png') }}" alt="Flowchart" style="max-width: 30%; height: auto;">


	<h2>Pseudocode for Player's Turn</h2>
	<pre>
Player's Turn:
    1. Deal initial cards to player and dealer
    2. Display player's hand and score
    3. While player's score is less than 21:
        a. Ask player to draw a card or stop
        b. If draw:
            i. Add a card to player's hand
            ii. Update player's score
            iii. Display new hand and score
        c. Else if stop:
            i. End player's turn
    </pre>

	<h2>Pseudocode for Dealer's Turn</h2>
	<pre>
Dealer's Turn:
    1. Deal initial cards to player and dealer
    2. While dealer's score is less than 17:
        a. Draw a card for dealer
        b. Update dealer's score
    3. End dealer's turn
    </pre>


	<h2>Class Descriptions</h2>
	<p>The following classes are used to represent different parts of the game:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Card:</strong>
			Represents a single card with a rank (e.g. 2-10, J, Q, K, A) and a suit (e.g. ♠', '♥', '♦', '♣'). Handles card values and string representation.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Deck:</strong>
			(Not explicitly shown, but implied) Would represent a deck of cards, shuffling and dealing cards to players and dealer.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Game:</strong>
			Manages the game logic, including the dealer's and player's turns, dealing cards, calculating scores, and checking for a winner.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>GameApiController:</strong>
			Provides a RESTful API for game status, like player score, dealer score, and remaining cards in the deck.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>GameController:</strong>
			Handles web routes for the game flow. It includes routes for starting the game, drawing cards, and dealer's turn. Also renders the main game interface and documentation.</li>
	</ul>

	<p>Back to
		<a href="{{ path('game_home') }}">Home</a>
	</p>
{% endblock %}
